    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44803" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔ-πλοος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, 
			contr.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔ-πλους</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ουν</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλέω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>good for sailing, fair</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔ. πλόος,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔπλοια</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Erinn.
				1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of a person,
				<i>having a fair voyage</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔπλοος ὅρμον ἵκοιτο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					7.62
				</span></i>
			 (-<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλοον</span> codd.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>BGU</u>
				665 ii 7
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(i A. D.)</span>.</div>
